Hi Guys!


It would be very nice if there was a default way
of users configuring automounted shares.

Now that the FUSE filesystem is on the kernel,
and users can mount whatever (and whichever) they
have access to, it would be nice if they could do
it automatically.


An awesome application for such a feature is that
one could write a GUI for FUSE, AutoMount and a
HAL which would *hopefully* make GnomeVFS and
KdeVFS obsolete (or at least less necessary)


What do you think about it ?
